      "comparison": "tolerance",
      "why": "Unlike the indices above, this runs pow(., 2.4) three times and a cube root up to three times, and neither language's library rounds those correctly. V8's Math.cbrt and CPython's t ** (1/3) differ by up to 1 ulp, and 500 * (f(x) - f(y)) amplifies that. Exact equality is not available and asserting it would make this table a tripwire for the libm, not for ARU.",
